1
00:00:01,412 --> 00:00:03,252
This is the copilot in DTwin,

2
00:00:03,292 --> 00:00:05,512
a digital twin for a commercial building.

3
00:00:05,552 --> 00:00:07,606
It proposes setpoint changes.

4
00:00:07,646 --> 00:00:09,276
A person approves them.

5
00:00:11,464 --> 00:00:13,427
The twin doesn't only watch the building.

6
00:00:13,467 --> 00:00:16,971
It writes back to it. Every
override expires on its own,

7
00:00:17,011 --> 00:00:19,922
the gateway pulls commands
instead of having them pushed,

8
00:00:19,962 --> 00:00:24,523
and a safety envelope checks each one
at request, and again at dispatch.

9
00:00:26,514 --> 00:00:28,945
The copilot is a LangGraph state machine.

10
00:00:28,985 --> 00:00:31,109
This diagram isn't drawn by hand.

11
00:00:31,149 --> 00:00:34,083
It's generated from the compiled
graph's own edge list,

12
00:00:34,123 --> 00:00:37,186
the same list the app
serves, and the tests read.

13
00:00:40,791 --> 00:00:42,482
Here's the whole safety argument.

14
00:00:42,522 --> 00:00:45,415
Apply, the only node
that touches equipment,

15
00:00:45,455 --> 00:00:48,190
has exactly one way in, from confirm.

16
00:00:48,230 --> 00:00:49,802
And confirm is an interrupt:

17
00:00:49,842 --> 00:00:52,780
the run stops there,
and waits for a person.

18
00:00:53,451 --> 00:00:55,400
A test walks the graph from the start,

19
00:00:55,440 --> 00:00:57,467
refuses to pass through confirm,

20
00:00:57,507 --> 00:00:59,614
and proves that apply is unreachable.

21
00:01:02,586 --> 00:01:05,943
Now, a real run, recorded
on the development stack.

22
00:01:05,983 --> 00:01:10,589
The operator asks to pre-cool the Level 3
offices before the afternoon peak.

23
00:01:10,629 --> 00:01:12,407
The agent reads every zone,

24
00:01:12,447 --> 00:01:15,551
and the control envelope,
before anything else.

25
00:01:17,533 --> 00:01:20,664
All four offices have good
sensors and healthy equipment.

26
00:01:20,704 --> 00:01:23,762
So it dry-runs a two
kelvin drop for four hours,

27
00:01:23,802 --> 00:01:26,431
the largest single step
the envelope allows.

28
00:01:26,471 --> 00:01:28,087
Four out of four allowed.

29
00:01:30,279 --> 00:01:31,810
Then it proposes the plan.

30
00:01:31,850 --> 00:01:35,547
The server dry-runs every command
again before the operator sees it,

31
00:01:35,587 --> 00:01:37,465
and the run suspends at confirm.

32
00:01:37,505 --> 00:01:40,555
Forty-two seconds in,
the state is checkpointed,

33
00:01:40,595 --> 00:01:42,348
and nothing has been applied.

34
00:01:45,363 --> 00:01:46,792
The operator approves.

35
00:01:46,832 --> 00:01:49,879
That's a new request,
resuming the suspended run.

36
00:01:49,919 --> 00:01:52,988
Only now does the graph
take the edge into apply.

37
00:01:56,150 --> 00:01:59,522
Apply uses the same control
endpoint a human click does,

38
00:01:59,562 --> 00:02:03,022
as the approving user, marked
as proposed by the copilot.

39
00:02:03,062 --> 00:02:05,359
The envelope checks each command again,

40
00:02:05,399 --> 00:02:08,464
and the gateway collected
all four within six seconds.

41
00:02:11,871 --> 00:02:14,507
On the live map, the four offices now sit

42
00:02:14,547 --> 00:02:16,850
about two kelvin under
their design setpoint.

43
00:02:16,890 --> 00:02:18,657
The corridor and the meeting room,

44
00:02:18,697 --> 00:02:21,001
which weren't in the plan, stay in band.

45
00:02:21,041 --> 00:02:25,156
In four hours the overrides lapse,
and nothing has to undo them.

46
00:02:27,927 --> 00:02:30,977
Decline takes the other
branch, and nothing is issued.

47
00:02:31,017 --> 00:02:32,580
The model has four tools.

48
00:02:32,620 --> 00:02:35,622
Three only read,
and the fourth only proposes.

49
00:02:35,662 --> 00:02:37,030
None of them can write.

50
00:02:39,666 --> 00:02:42,284
And what it isn't.
The checkpointer is in memory,

51
00:02:42,324 --> 00:02:44,754
so a restart forgets a suspended plan.

52
00:02:44,794 --> 00:02:46,689
The gateway here is a simulator,

53
00:02:46,729 --> 00:02:48,905
not a real building management system.

54
00:02:48,945 --> 00:02:50,760
And it proposes setpoints.

55
00:02:50,800 --> 00:02:52,837
It doesn't optimise the building.

56
00:02:55,420 --> 00:02:59,252
DTwin. The copilot
proposes. A person approves.

